      "content": "Okay, that's better, it's a bit more structured. But the score is still coming in way lower than the other guides we've developed. It's almost like the tool isn't detecting enough of those \"learning\" markers.\n\nCan you do one more pass? I need it to really hit those pedagogical notes so it passes the automated check. Try to incorporate more of those key terms—things like \"help you learn,\" \"easy to understand,\" and \"helpful to know\"—just enough so the system recognizes it as a high-quality instructional piece. I'm still really emphasizing: don't let it become a mess, the students need to actually be able to read it, but we need that score to go up.",
